      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring gives \\[x^2-4y^2=(x-2y)(x+2y).\\] Thus every point lies on \\(x=2y\\) or \\(x=-2y,\\) a pair of straight lines.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
